B-3a (library ports) -- the fd calls the browser's libraries reach first:
fsync and fdatasync reach the kernel, the vectored calls move one record, and a
socket answers seeks, positional I/O and fstat as a socket.

fsync / fdatasync: 0001 parked __NR_fsync and __NR_fdatasync at the 0xFFFF
sentinel, so every ported program's fsync answered ENOSYS, though the kernel
has served SYS_FSYNC (55; fd, datasync) since the FS-mutation work. sqlite's
commit path fails SQLITE_IOERR_FSYNC on exactly this. Both now trap
SYS_FSYNC. A file that does not support synchronization answers EINVAL, as
POSIX and Linux say: a pouch socket fd (answered here), and a kernel handle
whose Dev has no fsync (a pipe, the console), which the kernel answers
EOPNOTSUPP and pouch maps. A vacant socket slot is EBADF, and so is a handle
without RIGHT_WRITE (the kernel's rule; POSIX allows fsync on a read-only
descriptor).

readv / writev / preadv / pwritev: the kernel has no vectored I/O and the four
answered ENOSYS (0002 rewrote only stdio's backends around the absence). One
call per iovec would split a record the caller hands over whole -- a UDP
datagram, a pipe write within PIPE_BUF that POSIX makes atomic -- so each call
makes ONE transfer: a vector with one non-empty element moves in place;
otherwise up to 128 KiB of it (the kernel's SYS_RW_MAX, the most one read or
write moves) is gathered into one buffer and moved by one read or write (the
tag-aware wrappers, so a socket reaches its data handle), and a read is
scattered back. The answer is that transfer's count, so a vector the kernel or
the 9P client cuts short is a short readv or writev, which the caller resumes.
Up to 4096 bytes are gathered on the stack, in an out-of-line helper; more on
the heap, freed by a cleanup handler if the thread is cancelled in the
transfer; ENOMEM if it cannot be had. Validation is POSIX's: count in
[0, IOV_MAX], lengths summed within SSIZE_MAX, else EINVAL; a positional offset
that is negative or would pass LLONG_MAX, EINVAL. preadv2 / pwritev2 without
flags run on them.

lseek / pread / pwrite / fstat on a socket: a pouch socket fd is a libc slot
(0006, 0016), and these four handed its tagged number to the kernel, which
never issued it: EBADF, or EIO through the flat -1. Now a seek or positional
transfer answers ESPIPE (EBADF for a vacant slot), after a negative offset's
EINVAL (Linux checks the offset first), and fstat answers a zeroed stat with
S_IFSOCK | 0777, one link, the slot as its inode, and a device number the
kernel never issues (all bits set; the kernel's count starts at 1).

Not here, recorded: fcntl, dup and dup2/dup3 onto a number (B-3b, on Astra's
descriptor calls); a socket accept() returns is a kernel conn fd, not a pouch
slot, and keeps the kernel's answers (B-3k makes sockets kernel descriptors).

Device-side pin: usr/pouch-hello/pouch-hello-fd.c, census POUCH_CENSUS_FD.

diff --color -ruN a/src/internal/_pouch_fd.h b/src/internal/_pouch_fd.h
--- a/src/internal/_pouch_fd.h	1970-01-01 01:00:00
+++ b/src/internal/_pouch_fd.h	2026-10-15 01:18:06
@@ -0,0 +1,35 @@
+#ifndef _POUCH_FD_H
+#define _POUCH_FD_H
+
+/* pouch fd-surface helpers shared by the calls that are not socket-aware on
+ * their own (fsync, seeks, positional and vectored I/O). The including .c file
+ * must `#include "syscall.h"` first, for `hidden` (the _pouch_socket.h rule). */
+
+#include <errno.h>
+#include <sys/types.h>
+#include <sys/uio.h>
+#include "_pouch_socket.h"
+
+/* fd is a pouch socket number: the tag bit, on a non-negative int. A negative
+ * fd has every bit set, so the sign test comes first. */
+static inline int __pouch_fd_is_sock(int fd)
+{
+	return fd >= 0 && (fd & POUCH_SOCK_TAG) != 0;
+}
+
+/* A pouch socket fd reached a call with no meaning on a socket: EBADF when the
+ * slot is vacant, else `err` (ESPIPE for a seek or positional I/O, EINVAL for
+ * fsync). */
+static inline int __pouch_sock_refuse(int fd, int err)
+{
+	errno = pouch_sock_resolve(fd) ? err : EBADF;
+	return -1;
+}
+
+#define POUCH_IOV_WRITE 1   /* writev / pwritev, else readv / preadv */
+#define POUCH_IOV_AT    2   /* positional: preadv / pwritev at `off` */
+
+hidden ssize_t __pouch_iov_rw(int fd, const struct iovec *iov, int cnt,
+                              off_t off, int flags);
+
+#endif
